PilotApplyer Notice & Open-Source Attribution
==============================================

PilotApplyer is an independently maintained, customized, and deployed AI job discovery and automated application platform developed by Utsav Bechara.

This project incorporates and builds upon the open-source software project AIHawk (Jobs_Applier_AI_Agent), originally created by feder-cr and contributors under the MIT License.

Upstream Project Attribution
----------------------------
Original Repository: https://github.com/feder-cr/Jobs_Applier_AI_Agent
Original Copyright: Copyright (c) 2026 feder-cr

PilotApplyer includes or adapts work from the following upstream components:

1. Search Planner & Decision Engine
   - src/aihawk/profile.py, src/aihawk/database.py
   - The search plan's rules, multi-facet evaluation, and rarity weighting adapt the planner architecture of the upstream author's job-search engine.

2. Job Database & Ingestion Pipeline
   - pipeline/build.py, pipeline/publish.py, src/aihawk/library.py
   - Merged from public ATS feeds and datasets named in pipeline/build.py and docs/data-sources.md.
   - Job data from Headcount Labs (https://headcountlabs.com), licensed under ODbL 1.0, with geospatial location data from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL) and Overture Maps.
   - Forward Deployed Engineer postings from FDE Times, licensed under CC BY 4.0.
   - Each job posting remains the intellectual property of its respective employer and links back to original listings.

3. Browser Automation & Model Context Protocol (MCP)
   - src/aihawk/apply.py
   - Driven via invisible-playwright-mcp and Playwright browser automation engines.
